  {
    "lesson_id": "GAME-DOM-01",
    "beat_id": "define",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Here is the idea. Low dominates High for A if Low pays A more when B posts High, and Low still pays A more when B posts Low. Then High is dominated. A can delete it. You do not need to know what B will do.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\GAME-DOM-01\\audio\\en\\define.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "GAME-DOM-01",
    "beat_id": "matrix",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Read A's numbers only. If B posts High, A gets 3 from High and 5 from Low. If B posts Low, A gets 0 from High and 1 from Low. Five beats three. One beats zero. Low dominates High for A.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\GAME-DOM-01\\audio\\en\\matrix.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "GAME-DOM-01",
    "beat_id": "example",
    "language": "en",
    "text": "People stop after one column. Do not. Low must beat High against every board B might post. One column is a hint. Both columns is a dominant strategy.",
    "dest_path": "C:\\Users\\kochi\\Dropbox\\video-factory\\out\\GAME-DOM-01\\audio\\en\\example.mp3",
    "with_timestamps": true
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "GAME-DOM-01",
    "beat_id": "takeaway",
